From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CatPieLeaf <catpieleaf@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 09 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] nv-vm: fix RSS accounting against 7.2's lazy_percpu_counter

7.2 reworked mm_struct RSS accounting:

  -	struct percpu_counter      rss_stat[NR_MM_COUNTERS];
  +	struct lazy_percpu_counter rss_stat[NR_MM_COUNTERS];

nv_account_mm_alloc()/nv_account_mm_free() still poke rss_stat directly.
Their NV_PERCPU_MM_COUNTER conftest no longer matches the new type, so
both fall through to the pre-percpu branch, which treats the array as a
struct:

  nv-vm.c:989:51: error: member reference base type
                  'struct lazy_percpu_counter[4]' is not a structure or union
  nv-vm.c:1003:71: error: member reference base type
                  'struct lazy_percpu_counter[4]' is not a structure or union

The obvious replacement, add_mm_counter_other(), cannot be used from a
module: it is a static inline that ends with mm_trace_rss_stat(), and
that function is not exported, so the module links but modpost rejects
it:

  ERROR: modpost: "mm_trace_rss_stat" [nvidia.ko] undefined!

Call lazy_percpu_counter_add_atomic() directly instead. It is the same
counter update add_mm_counter_other() performs, is a pure static inline
over atomics and percpu_counter_add() - which resolves to the exported
percpu_counter_add_batch() - and so is safe from a module. The only
thing given up is the rss_stat tracepoint firing for these two
allocations; the counters themselves stay correct.

The atomic variant is the right one here rather than the _fast()/local
path: both call sites operate on an mm pinned with mmgrab() rather than
current->mm, and the free path runs from a workqueue.

Older kernels keep the existing conftest branches untouched, so this
stays buildable against < 7.2. LINUX_VERSION_CODE and KERNEL_VERSION are
already in scope through nv-linux.h, which nv-vm.c includes and which
uses them itself.

Signed-off-by: CatPieLeaf <catpieleaf@proton.me>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia/nv-vm.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-vm.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-vm.c
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-vm.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-vm.c
@@ -983,7 +983,9 @@
     mm_work->mm = mm;
     mm_work->num_pages = numPages;
     mmgrab(mm);
-#if defined(NV_PERCPU_MM_COUNTER)
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(7, 2, 0)
+    lazy_percpu_counter_add_atomic(&mm->rss_stat[MM_SHMEMPAGES], numPages);
+#elif defined(NV_PERCPU_MM_COUNTER)
     percpu_counter_add(&mm->rss_stat[MM_SHMEMPAGES], numPages);
 #else
     atomic_long_add_return(numPages, &mm->rss_stat.count[MM_SHMEMPAGES]);
@@ -997,7 +999,10 @@
     {
         return;
     }
-#if defined(NV_PERCPU_MM_COUNTER)
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(7, 2, 0)
+    lazy_percpu_counter_add_atomic(&mm_work->mm->rss_stat[MM_SHMEMPAGES],
+                                   -mm_work->num_pages);
+#elif defined(NV_PERCPU_MM_COUNTER)
     percpu_counter_add(&mm_work->mm->rss_stat[MM_SHMEMPAGES], -mm_work->num_pages);
 #else
     atomic_long_add_return(-mm_work->num_pages, &mm_work->mm->rss_stat.count[MM_SHMEMPAGES]);
-- 
